    questionText: "(a) Draw a large freehand sketch of the given house and, on your sketch, show the pipework necessary to supply hot water from the stove to the radiators and to heat the water in the cylinder. Include the following in your sketch: wood pellet stove; hot water cylinder; pipework to and from the cylinder; expansion tank / vessel; pipework to radiators; all necessary pumps and valves. (b) Discuss one advantage of installing a zoned heating system so the radiators and hot water can be heated separately.",
