    questionText: "(a) To a scale of 1:5, draw a vertical section through the external wall and bottom portion of the window. Show the typical construction details from a level 400 mm below to a level 300 mm above the concrete window cill. Include three typical dimensions on your drawing. (b) Show on your drawing the typical design detailing to prevent water entering at the window cill.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 50,
    rows: [
    { id: "a-details", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Any 7 x 5 marks", marks: 35, contextNote: "Credit the best SEVEN acceptable details at 5 marks each, capped at 35. Marked details: block outer leaf; full-fill insulated cavity; wall ties; block inner leaf; 13 mm plaster and 19 mm render; cavity closer; DPC; precast concrete cill with throating/drip; window board; airtight tape; window frame 120 × 80 mm; triple glazing.", permittedMarks: [0,5,10,15,20,25,30,35] },
    { id: "a-dimensions", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Any three typical dimensions", marks: 3, contextNote: "Three appropriate typical dimensions on the section, 1 each.", permittedMarks: [0,1,2,3] },
    { id: "a-presentation", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Draughting, accuracy and scale (excellent, good, fair)", marks: 8, contextNote: "Draughting, accuracy and scale of the section: excellent 8, good 6, fair 4.", permittedMarks: [0,4,6,8] },
    { id: "b-cill", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "Throating / drip / DPC", marks: 4, contextNote: "Show and identify the detail, such as a sloped cill overhanging the render with a throating or drip, wrapped in DPC. Any other suitable detail is accepted.", permittedMarks: [0,4] },
    ],
